WEBVTT

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.020
Don't bother me!

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.640
What's your problem?!

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.830
You're bothering the other passengers if you act like a jerk.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:51.890
Shut up!
You're bothering the other passengers if you act like a jerk.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.030
No, you shut up!

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.110
What?

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.330
Come on, stop it.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:57.890
Cut me some slack.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:58.450
Shut up!
Cut me some slack.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:58.910
Shut up!

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.440
What?

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.450
Hey!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.040
Huh?

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.290
Is that so?

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.220
Something stinks here.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.850
Don't touch me!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.680
How uncool.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.830
What are you doing?

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.330
You?

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.550
Have we met before?

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:55.300
Bastard.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.510
Transform.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.520
How is Tagami Shikei doing?

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.320
He can't move yet.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.700
Just like you wanted, I have strengthened a function of your weapon as a catalyst.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.640
Thank you, Bishop Aragami.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:18.120
Could you explain that new mission to me?

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:23.430
In the next battle I'm planning to open a Zadan.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.920
Because my lack of experience caused Itsuki and Tagami Shikei to get hurt.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:40.210
We should worry about one man capable of eliminating a Contracted Priest's work.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.470
I'm going to send Isaki to the area as a new defender.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.470
But, there is more.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.170
I would like you to send Bishop Sougi there, too.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.170
Understood.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.510
The Great Bishop is also worried about that.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.440
Vice Great Bishop, I have something to ask you.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.180
It is still uncertain who shot Akasha...

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.070
And there is a rumor that...

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.010
...the Kougon-cult allows several priests to give the death penalty to even humans, so I was wondering if...

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.010
Buddha's teachings tell us...

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.820
...that there is no way to kill a man.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.120
It must have been five years.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.050
One day a powerful Corpse appeared and caused a rampage.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.830
They started a punitive expedition.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.650
Akasha was in that punitive expedition too.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.160
We thought it was just an normal fight.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.640
But soon we lost touch with the expedition.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:58.290
What the backup priests who rushed over there saw that day...

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:08.170
...was only one surviving Contracted Priest and his defeated Shikabane Hime.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.800
He was standing embracing the remaining half of his Shikabane Hime's body.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:19.480
They saw the hellish eyes of Akasha.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:33.120
After investigating, nobody understood what happened that day.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.180
Soon after I was suspended from the investigation.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.220
But...

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.040
One week later.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:50.130
He murdered his own Shikabane Hime, killed many priests and stole the Sutra.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.140
And I heard he appeared frequently here and there.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.210
I don't know why,

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.760
but I thought there was no wonder he did those things.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:08.290
Are you sympathizing with a man who murdered his own Shikabane Hime?

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:18.740
Yes?

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.020
This is the Partenon.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:21.700
Master?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:22.460
Is that you, Oori?

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.020
What's the matter?

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:23.120
Sign: Kendo Dojo.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.410
I'm sorry to bother you.
Sign: Kendo Dojo.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:24.930
Sign: Kendo Dojo.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.580
My brother isn't feeling well.
Sign: Kendo Dojo.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.950
I wondered if it's possible to get the day off.
Sign: Kendo Dojo.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.110
That's all right.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.560
There aren't any clients anyway.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:33.960
Yes.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.010
I hope his wounds aren't too bad.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.170
Are you all right?

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.940
It's nothing really.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.300
Hope he gets well soon.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:44.300
Strange.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.550
I can't remember telling him he got hurt.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:48.230
Did someone get hurt?

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.230
Just my brother.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.370
By the way.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.340
What is it that you want to show me?

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.800
Think carefully before you speak.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.450
It got in my side!

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.450
A blog?

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.240
Yeah.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:02.830
Flag: Victory Taikai High School

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.640
We went to the same kendo club in middle school.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.110
You got wounded again?!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.390
I fell off my bike while delivering the newspapers.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:19.310
So your friend wrote that blog?

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.530
Y...Yeah.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.250
He stopped coming to school in the second year though.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:26.730
He dropped out of school?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.520
There was a dumb senpai tormenting his underlings.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.110
Huh?

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:42.940
This seems like a novel, not a blog.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.770
It used to be a diary about his video games.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.800
And the teacher picked on him every day.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.700
The blog turned weird from that day on.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.240
Birth?

00:08:56.030 --> 00:09:02.590
It's normal that the people from the kendo club, my parents or relatives couldn't understand me.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.430
Now I'm just drowning in my own pity.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.640
It is me who has been chosen, not them.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:13.170
I'll use this power for the sake of this world.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:18.050
A senpai from the kendo club died recently.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.140
Did he bully you guys?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.140
I heard he got hit by a train.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.530
I'm sure it's just a coincidence, but...

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:31.060
I tried to contact Mitsuyoshi, this blog's writer, but I didn't get any answer.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:35.550
Why are you telling me this?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:36.470
Oori?

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Inuhiko talked to you about Corpses before right?

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.960
You know, the rumor about people who die but don't want to, and turn into monster called a Corpse.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.590
It may be just a myth, but in the temples they talk about stuff like that.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:50.740
I know nothing about that!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.640
It's not good to believe such things.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:55.750
You're right.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.050
And Mitsuyoshi couldn't possibly be dead.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:06.920
That guy...

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:11.240
...writing the blog must surely have turned into a Corpse after dying of electrocution.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.750
But he hasn't realized it yet.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.710
Why did you lie?

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:26.270
I lied in the same way as my brother did about my wounds and about Corpses.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.040
But that was to protect my friends.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:31.810
But you're just a normal human too.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.720
I'll leave the Corpses to my brother and Hoshimura-san.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.890
There is nothing I can do.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.010
It's just like you said.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:59.330
I involved Keisei for my own convenience.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.200
But that's because...

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.030
Not because you want to go to heaven, right?

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.310
Probably.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.970
I don't know what Keisei told you.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:23.810
I am looking for the Corpses that murdered me and my family.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:29.150
I am here only to kill those Corpses.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.320
So don't misunderstand.

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:38.180
We are no heroes or protectors of justice.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.870
If you stay with us, someday you...

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.170
...and Keisei will die.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:52.590
But...

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:58.160
Hey, there is one more thing I'd like to ask you.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.950
Hoshimura-san, are you my brother’s...

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:03.730
...girlfriend?

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.490
She sure scared me.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:12.920
Hoshimura-san never tolerates anything.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.390
I wasn't able to talk about that blog.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.710
Are you dead?

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.790
Mitsuyoshi?

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.100
I remember him.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:55.100
By the way, you're making a pass?

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:55.700
No.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.520
I just wanted to know about Mitsuyoshi-kun.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:59.520
I understand, I understand.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.340
What is it, priest?

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.410
Do you want some money for the offering box?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.620
Sit on it, you troublemakers.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.680
Bastard!

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.210
Isaki-san!

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:14.490
Let's get out of this dangerous place.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.240
Don't give me orders.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:19.530
What did you find out after talking to those fools?

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:31.130
Isaki-san.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.850
Note: Shuugodai is a guardian of a particular area.
Call me Shuugodai-sama.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:37.330
Until Tagami Shikei's wounds are healed, I'll be Shuugodai-sama.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.310
It's our chance to get promoted.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:40.760
Do you understand?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.230
Shuugodai-sama.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.080
Strange taste.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.720
An idiot made a comment in the Corpse's blog.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:02.510
If he is a Corpse, we must dispose of him at all cost.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.950
We'll kill another three this month.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:13.910
What does this mean?

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:21.530
You really came?

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.390
You must be Mitsuyoshi-kun.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.420
What did you mean when you asked if I was dead?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.380
Nobody will come here.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.410
And we won't cause any trouble here.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.660
So please listen to what I have to say.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:45.260
That boy is surely...

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.040
It’s Tagami Shikei's little brother.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:49.040
He is getting himself in trouble lately.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.350
The head temple are still suspecting him.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.200
It's a great opportunity.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.520
Let's watch over this.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.440
But...

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:01.770
You must know Sumitori.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.280
Sumi...

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:07.270
tori…

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:10.300
Sumitori was worrying about you.

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:13.930
He said you were writing strange things on your blog.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.070
I bet he would worry about me.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.500
Sumitori was also ignoring me.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.170
Mitsuyoshi-kun?

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:29.650
If you have truly become a hero,

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:34.660
you must find another way of doing things.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.040
Mitsuyoshi-kun?!

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:50.840
I...

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:51.670
Mitsuyoshi-kun!

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.480
Transform!

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.040
Corpse!

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:04.090
Who are you?

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:09.070
I'm here to destroy Corpses that can't forget this world like you.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:10.490
I’m a Shikabane Hime!

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.250
You too?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:18.990
In other words, you are evil.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.530
Evil?

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.900
I am not what you call a Corpse.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.760
I am a hero who has been granted a new life to do great things.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.780
Minai!

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:33.780
What are you doing?

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.200
Attack at once!

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.530
Yes, Isaki-san.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.530
I won't tolerate evil.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.180
I won't tolerate those hurting people.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.910
And you, who are trying to kill me, are evil!

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.960
Corpses are not allowed to exist.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.500
I am different!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.180
I am justice!

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:05.860
Minai!

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.320
It is cursed.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:10.930
Cursed?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:14.390
Not only did that Corpse change in something huge and powerful because of his own delusion.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.730
He also has a special ability.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.540
That curse enables him to use telekinesis.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.840
Are you my brother's...

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:26.390
You're in my way!

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:27.910
What's wrong, Minai?!

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:28.960
Please wait!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.960
She's getting hurt more than the Corpse.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:31.730
At this rate she'll...

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.190
Shut up!

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:36.240
If you strained him a little bit longer we could have gotten him in one hit!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.270
You troublemaker!

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.800
Stand up, Minai!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:40.660
Isaki-san!

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:07.060
What's wrong?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.580
Try and attack me!

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:13.820
I don't feel any of your attacks.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.350
I am justice.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.270
You are evil!

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:19.950
Out of the way!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.740
I'll defeat that cursed one!

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:35.870
I get it.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:39.660
He can reflect the damage he got on the same place of his opponent's body.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.640
Is that your curse?!

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:52.870
Minai!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.660
Don't misunderstand!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.430
We are no heroes or protectors of justice.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.900
If you stay with us, you'll die someday.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:30.970
You were reckless, Oori-san.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.880
Please rest out here for a while.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:39.640
Isaki Daisoujou and I will take it from here.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.010
Why do you listen to that man?

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:47.910
Because he is my Contracted Priest

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.570
I...

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:53.250
...killed a man.

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.240
I was going to die together with him.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:05.870
But I didn't die.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.390
That is why I am taking this penalty.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.590
Was becoming a Shikabane Hime a punishment?

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.120
It's just like that Corpse said.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.960
He is justice.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.850
And maybe we are all evil.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.040
That can't be true.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:34.810
That Isaki-san wanted to get rid of me, but you came to save me.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:37.250
That's because I couldn't just stand there and watch.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:39.790
Thank you.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:45.950
So here you are.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:50.010
Minai!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.690
Just like I thought.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.180
Hoshimura-san?

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:11.130
I didn't receive any damage when I attacked its right arm.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.500
I'm glad I'm missing mine.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:17.990
Why are you here?

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:21.180
The head temple asked about your cell phone.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:24.610
They wanted to know why you were at the same place as Isaki-san.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.020
Why did you show up again?

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:29.560
So that's why you got worried about me.

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:29.950
Yes.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.880
Thank you, hero.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:42.800
You're such an idiot.

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:28.070
Who are you shedding those tears for?

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:34.500
Isn't this just one more wounded body in a world of pain?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:38.560
Congratulate on attaining peace.
